  "caption": "Quinn bought a kettlebell and planned 100 swings with no warm-up. By swing 87 the back sent a memo, and the cleans kept bonking the wrist.\n\nSwings aren't bad for your back. Most kettlebell niggles come from swinging with the back instead of the hips, going overhead without shoulder control, the bell flipping onto the wrist, and fatigue.\n\nWhat can help: learning the hip hinge without a bell, letting the hips drive while the arms guide, starting lighter and building shoulder control before overhead work, ending the set when form breaks, and getting coaching for cleans and snatches.\n\nGet it checked if you have an existing back or shoulder problem, wrist pain from the bell, or pain that keeps hanging around.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
